      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right—rest won't resurrect a spark that's been extinguished by a lost sense of purpose. If the world feels heavy and gray, maybe the point isn't to find color again, but to learn how to sit with the gray and let it shape something honest. You don't have to create for the world's sake; you can create simply to see what your own silence has to say. And if nothing comes, that's not failure—it's just a different season of being.",
